# AA-993 V4 (ADR 0016 D3) — rows of the TripPlanner web (ECS behind CloudFront) post-deploy verify, read by
# .github/scripts/post_deploy_verify.sh web. BASE = the public production host (no deployment protection there).
#
# One row per line: name|kind|target|expected|jq assertion
#   kind public: target "GET <path>", expected = HTTP code, assertion = jq on the body that must be true (empty =
#   only the HTTP code). Variables: $sha (the deployed commit, deploy-web-dev.yml github.sha) and
#   $version (.release-please-manifest.json of that commit). {cb} = a fresh cache-buster per try.
# A row fails after VERIFY_TRIES tries (the web verify uses more: the ECS rollout may still be settling). A PR that adds
# or changes a route worth guarding adds a row here.
#
# /api/health (AA-891) answers what deploy-web-dev.yml baked into THIS image (build args GIT_SHA / APP_VERSION), so a
# match proves the public host serves the image of this run.

health|public|GET /api/health?_cb={cb}|200|.status == "ok" and .service == "aa-tripplanner-web" and .git_sha == $sha and .version == $version
